---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="For Parents | Credits That Count"
  description="For parents: help your student check college credits before enrolling, paying tuition, or repeating a course, and verify what a college tells you against published sources."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="block" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <h1>For parents</h1>
      <p>
        You do not have to take a college's word for it. The checker reads
        Louisiana's published transfer rules and shows you, course by
        course, what counts at the college your student chooses, whether
        the course is already finished or still being planned. Pick where
        to start:
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="pathgrid">
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/#check-credits">
          <span class="pathbox-title">Match College Credits</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">See which of your student's courses count at the college they choose.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/#compare">
          <span class="pathbox-title">Compare Two Colleges</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Put two colleges side by side on the same courses.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/#what-to-take-next">
          <span class="pathbox-title">What to Take Next</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">See which courses keep your student on track.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/#admission">
          <span class="pathbox-title">Admission Check</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Check the admission standards for the college your student wants.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/checker/#coverage-colleges">
          <span class="pathbox-title">Coverage</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">See which colleges are covered, and request the ones being built.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p>
        Every answer names its published source, so you can check before
        enrolling, before paying tuition, or before your student repeats a
        course. Only the receiving college makes the final decision on how
        a credit applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/checker/">Open the Checker</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
